   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Three classes, not three pronouncements",
   "texto": [
    "There are 44 traditional consonant letters; two are almost obsolete. To read current words it is appropriate to recognize the other 42. They are grouped into **clase media**, **alta** and **baja**. The class does not in itself indicate how to pronounce the consonant: it helps to calculate the tone of the syllable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Letras and sounds",
   "texto": [
    "Several letters can represent the same initial sound. For example, **ข** and **ค** start with a sound similar to «k», but they belong to different classes and therefore can give different tones. Learn each letter along with your class; do not try to deduce it by sound alone."
   ]
